    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/tarball/v2.3.0",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/zipball/v2.3.0",
    "body": "`pip install -U mcp`. Docs: https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/\r\n\r\nMostly fixes, plus three new options. A few things behave differently, so skim these first:\r\n\r\n## Behaviour changes\r\n\r\n**`httpx2>=2.10.0` is now required** (#3600)\r\n- It was `>=2.5.0`. The new `max_sse_event_size` option needs it.\r\n- Nothing to do unless you pin `httpx2` below 2.10.\r\n\r\n**A tool with an invalid `x-mcp-header` annotation fails at registration** (#3620)\r\n- `@mcp.tool()`, `add_tool` and `Tool.from_function` raise `InvalidSignature`, naming the tool and the problem.\r\n- Until now the server started, and 2026-07-28 clients silently dropped the tool from their listing.\r\n- Refused: anything other than a plain `str`, `int` or `bool` parameter (so also `str | None`, `float`, lists and enums), a header name that isn't a valid token, and two names that differ only by case.\r\n- For an optional header parameter, give the schema directly: `Annotated[str | None, WithJsonSchema({\"type\": \"string\", \"x-mcp-header\": \"Region\"})] = None`.\r\n\r\n**Empty `_meta` and `params` are no longer sent** (#3628)\r\n- On 2025-11-25 and earlier connections, 2.x sent `\"_meta\": {}` on every request. Some servers reject that. It is now left out, as in v1.\r\n- `ping` and list requests without a cursor go out with no `params` member.\r\n- On the receiving side `ctx.meta` is `None` rather than `{}`, and middleware sees `ctx.params` as `None` for a request without params.\r\n- 2026-07-28 connections are unchanged.\r\n\r\n**`initialize` leaves out `experimental` when none is configured** (#3614)\r\n- It used to send `\"experimental\": {}`. `server/discover` already left it out.\r\n- Client code reading `capabilities.experimental` on a legacy connection should handle `None`.\r\n\r\n**`Mcp-Param-*` validation looks the tool up by name** (#3630)\r\n- `MCPServer` no longer runs `tools/list` for every `tools/call`, so middleware no longer sees that extra request.\r\n- The registered schema is what gets checked. Middleware that filters or rewrites `tools/list` no longer affects it.\r\n\r\n**An interactive OAuth login no longer counts against request timeouts** (#3635)\r\n- The timeout pauses while `OAuthClientProvider` waits on `redirect_handler` and `callback_handler`.\r\n- This fixes `Client(mode=\"auto\")` settling on `2025-11-25` when the login took longer than 10 seconds.\r\n- A request timeout no longer ends a login nobody finishes. Put a limit inside `callback_handler` if you need one.\r\n\r\n## New\r\n\r\n- `max_sse_event_size=` on `streamable_http_client` and `StreamableHttpParameters`. The default stays 1 MiB per SSE event; raise it, or pass `None`, for larger tool results (#3600).\r\n- `MCPServer(subscriptions=False)` stops serving `subscriptions/listen` and advertises `listChanged` and `subscribe` as false (#3626).\r\n- `Server(get_tool_input_schema=...)` lets a low-level server supply a tool's schema for header validation without running its `tools/list` handler (#3630).\r\n- `Client.call_tool` re-lists the tools and retries once after a `HeaderMismatch` (`-32020`) rejection (#3627).\r\n\r\n## Fixes\r\n\r\n- `ctx: Context[AppState]` works on prompts and resource templates, not only on tools (#3624).\r\n- An explicit `\"structuredContent\": null` is checked against the output schema instead of being treated as missing (#3621).\r\n- A `progress_callback` that raises no longer fails the call on an in-process `Client(server)` (#3623).\r\n- Client OpenTelemetry spans record JSON-RPC error responses. With `mode=\"auto\"`, connecting to a server without `server/discover` now shows one `ERROR` span for the probe (#3629).\r\n- `stdio_client` resolves the executable off the event loop on Windows (#3510).\r\n\r\n## Docs\r\n\r\n- New pages: [Cancellation](https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/handlers/cancellation/) and [Header parameters](https://py.sdk.modelcontextprotocol.io/advanced/header-parameters/), plus a middleware tutorial.\r\n- All twelve translations are refreshed (#3636).\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* Detect event-loop blocking in tests by @Kludex in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3510\r\n* Bump httpcore2 from 2.5.0 to 2.10.0 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3482\r\n* Ask cubic for a review when the intake gate lets a PR back in by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3489\r\n* docs: remove v2 notice from top of README by @claude[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3604\r\n* Bump anyio from 4.10.0 to 4.14.2 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3547\r\n* Make the deeply nested body test independent of stack size by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3610\r\n* Fall back to an NTFS junction when the symlink escape test can't create a symlink by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3609\r\n* Group Dependabot security updates for uv dependencies by @Kludex in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3611\r\n* Expose an SSE event size limit in Streamable HTTP clients by @Kludex in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3600\r\n* Bump the github-actions group with 5 updates by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3612\r\n* docs: add a middleware tutorial that refuses tool calls by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3613\r\n* Omit an unset experimental capability from the initialize result by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3614\r\n* Document when a caller-supplied request id can be minted again by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3619\r\n* Document the timeout a hand-built httpx2 client needs by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3618\r\n* Reject a tool with an invalid x-mcp-header annotation at registration by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3620\r\n* Validate an explicit null structuredContent against the output schema by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3621\r\n* Contain a raising progress callback on the in-process dispatcher by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3623\r\n* Keep the live Context when a prompt or template annotates Context[T] by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3624\r\n* Describe the ID-JAG confidential-client rule as SDK policy, not a SEP-990 requirement by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3622\r\n* Let MCPServer opt out of serving subscriptions/listen by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3626\r\n* Document how a handler deals with cancellation by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3625\r\n* Omit an empty _meta and empty params from outbound requests by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3628\r\n* Record JSON-RPC error responses on the client OpenTelemetry span by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3629\r\n* Retry a tool call once after a HeaderMismatch rejection by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3627\r\n* Look the tool schema up by name for Mcp-Param-* validation instead of running tools/list by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3630\r\n* Bump urllib3 from 2.7.0 to 2.8.0 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3607\r\n* Let a newer Deploy Docs run cancel the one in progress by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3633\r\n* Link What's new to the Header parameters page by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3632\r\n* Keep inline-snapshot disabled when pytest runs in a terminal by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3634\r\n* Stop counting an interactive OAuth login against request timeouts by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3635\r\n* docs: refresh translations for recent English changes by @maxisbey in https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3636\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v2.2.0...v2.3.0",
    "mentions_count": 4
  },
